IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art18-governor-duties`
IMPORT `g6-art19-reportable-matters`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`
IMPORT `ind-b-tests-fixtures-g6`

-- ind-b-tests-art18-20: independent tests of Articles 18 to 20 (group G6), by test author ind-b.
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the Law before this module's imports were opened; each assertion cites its row id.
-- A section headed "reading checks" tests a non-default reading of a fork against what that reading itself says.

§ `Article 18 -- duties of governors (rows E18-01 to E18-18)`

-- E18-01: every governor of a registered charity owes the 18(1) duties; none where the entity is not registered.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` FALSE)
-- E18-02: a governor of a registered 2(1)(i) unincorporated association owes the 18(2) standard.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `an unincorporated body or association of persons`))
-- E18-03: a governor of a registered company does not.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`))
-- E18-04: a governor of an unregistered association does not.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `ind-b6 A` FALSE (`ind-b6 entity` `not on the register` `an unincorporated body or association of persons`))
-- E18-05: a trustee of a registered trust does not.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `the trustees of a trust`))
-- E18-06: a constitution that excuses due diligence is overridden.
#ASSERT `Art 18(3) the provision of the constitution is overridden by the duties of this Article` TRUE FALSE
-- E18-07: a constitution imposing a more onerous duty is not overridden.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 18(3) the provision of the constitution is overridden by the duties of this Article` TRUE TRUE
-- E18-08, E18-09: the governor's own contravention or offence within 2(10) (a tax offence about the charity, 2(10)(b)(iii)).
#ASSERT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` FALSE (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" TRUE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- E18-10: concurs in the charity's misconduct.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` TRUE (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE TRUE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- E18-11: encourages another governor, who engages in misconduct.
#ASSERT `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `ind-b6 A` FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conduct` "B. Encourager" FALSE FALSE (LIST "C. Wrongdoer") FALSE FALSE FALSE), (`ind-b6 conduct` "C. Wrongdoer" TRUE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE)) (`ind-b6 conduct` "B. Encourager" FALSE FALSE (LIST "C. Wrongdoer") FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- E18-12, E18-16, E18-18: ought to have become aware; failed to take proper steps within a reasonable time.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` FALSE (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- E18-13: aware of another's intention; actively conceals it.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` FALSE (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- E18-14: aware; took proper steps in time; no concealment: not misconduct.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` FALSE (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- E18-15: neither aware nor ought to have been: not misconduct under (d).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` FALSE (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- E18-17: none of (a) to (d).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` TRUE `ind-b6 innocent`

§ `Article 19(1) -- reportable matters (rows E19-01 to E19-16)`

-- E19-01, E19-02: misconduct as governor that led to a required steps notice.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `ind-b6 A` (LIST `ind-b6 an unmet notice`) (`ind-b6 a governor whose own misconduct, with a notice served, led` TRUE)
-- E19-03: misconduct, no notice from it: not (a).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` `ind-b6 A` (LIST `ind-b6 an unmet notice`) (`ind-b6 a governor whose own misconduct, with a notice served, led` FALSE)
-- E19-04: subject of a disqualification order in force.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` (LIST (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2030 1 1))) FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
-- E19-05: another restriction under this Law.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY TRUE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
-- E19-06, E19-07: disqualified as a charity trustee (UK, or an equivalent elsewhere).
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `ind-b6 A` (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE (LIST `ind-b6 a disqualification of 2020 with no end`) EMPTY FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
-- E19-08, E19-09: disqualified as a company director (or an equivalent outside Jersey).
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(d) the person has been disqualified as a company director or from an equivalent position` `ind-b6 A` (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE EMPTY (LIST `ind-b6 a disqualification of 2020 with no end`) FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
-- E19-10: bankrupt or otherwise insolvent.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `ind-b6 A` EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY TRUE EMPTY FALSE) EQUALS LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`
-- E19-11: a SPENT conviction under this Law.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `ind-b6 A` EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE)) FALSE) EQUALS LIST `a conviction, whether or not spent, for an offence under this Law`
-- E19-12: an unspent conviction under this Law.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(f) the person has a conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law` (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE)) FALSE)
-- E19-13: an unspent conviction for a 2(10)(b) offence.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `ind-b6 A` EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE)) FALSE) EQUALS LIST `an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)`
-- E19-14: a SPENT conviction for a 2(10)(b) offence not under this Law: not reportable.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `ind-b6 A` EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conviction` FALSE TRUE TRUE)) FALSE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- E19-15: a prescribed description.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(h) the person falls within another description prescribed by Order` (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY TRUE)
-- E19-16: none.
#ASSERT `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` `ind-b6 A` EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 1) `ind-b6 a clean person` EQUALS EMPTY

§ `Article 19(2) to (8) -- reports, declarations, statement (rows E19-17 to E19-29)`

-- E19-17: a governor of a registered charity with a reportable matter must report it to the charity AND the Commissioner; both reports discharge it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` TRUE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`)))
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` TRUE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`))) 0 (LIST EVENT `a governor` (`report the reportable matter to the entity or charity` `a governor`) 1, EVENT `a governor` (`report the reportable matter to the Commissioner` `a governor`) 2))
-- E19-18: a report to the charity only does not discharge it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` TRUE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`))) 0 (LIST EVENT `a governor` (`report the reportable matter to the entity or charity` `a governor`) 1))
-- E19-19: a governor of an applicant: the same duty.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` FALSE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 applicant` `a company`) (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`)))
-- E19-20: a governor of an applicant with no reportable matter must declare before the application.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 applicant` `a company`) (`ind-b6 governor` "H. Clean" EMPTY) (YMD 2026 1 10))
#ASSERT `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `ind-b6 A` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)) (YMD 2026 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `ind-b6 A` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 15)) (YMD 2026 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `ind-b6 A` NOTHING (YMD 2026 1 10)
-- E19-21: a governor of a registered charity with no reportable matter, notified: must declare.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 governor` "H. Clean" EMPTY) TRUE)
-- E19-22: the application states the declarations, all held: complied; the application is complete as far as 19(6) goes.
#ASSERT `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` TRUE (LIST (`ind-b6 position` "H. Clean" FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(6) the application is not complete for want of Article 19(5)` TRUE
-- E19-23: no statement: not complete.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 position` "H. Clean" FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `Art 19(6) the application is not complete for want of Article 19(5)` FALSE
-- E19-24: three governors, one reported and two declared: complied.
#ASSERT `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` TRUE (LIST (`ind-b6 position` "G. Brown" TRUE FALSE), (`ind-b6 position` "H. Clean" FALSE TRUE), (`ind-b6 position` "I. Clean" FALSE TRUE))
-- E19-25: three governors, one reported, one declared, one neither: not complied, so not complete.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` TRUE (LIST (`ind-b6 position` "G. Brown" TRUE FALSE), (`ind-b6 position` "H. Clean" FALSE TRUE), (`ind-b6 position` "J. Silent" FALSE FALSE))
-- E19-26: a registered charity's annual return without the statement: contravenes 19(5), and must explain the reason.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(5) the registered charity has stated in its annual return that it holds declarations` FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 position` "H. Clean" FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(7) the registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain the reason to the Commissioner` FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(7) the registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain the reason to the Commissioner` TRUE)
-- E19-27: a governor with an unreported reportable matter is in breach of 19(2), must not act (19(8)), is outside 19(10), and commits no 19(11) offence; 19(8) carries no penalty.
#ASSERT `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` `ind-b6 A` NOTHING `ind-b6 day` (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`)) (`ind-b6 reports` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 reports` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE) EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` (`Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 reports` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE) EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE) FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 19(8) the penalty for contravening Article 19(8)` `ind-b6 A` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, `no fine is provided`)
-- E19-28: a governor with no reportable matter, notified, who has not declared: in breach of 19(4), so barred by 19(8).
#ASSERT `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 day` (`ind-b6 governor` "H. Clean" EMPTY) (`Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)), NOTHING, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- E19-29: neither (2) nor (4) breached (only (3), for an applicant): no 19(8) bar.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Article 19(9) to (13) (rows E19-30 to E19-48)`

-- E19-30, E19-31: on a report, the Commissioner must inquire and may apply to the court.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(9)(a) the Commissioner must make inquiries into whether the governor is a fit and proper person` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(9)(b) the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine the issue` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- E19-32: issue undetermined: the application may not be granted.
#ASSERT `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- E19-33: determined, resulting notice not complied with: still barred.
#ASSERT `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- E19-34: determined and complied with: no longer barred.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (LIST (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- E19-35: a registered charity: the Commissioner MAY permit the governor to act pending determination.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(9)(d) the Commissioner may permit the governor to act until the issue is determined` TRUE (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- E19-36: not before the court: the Commissioner must serve a notice requiring removal, or permit by notice in the register; either discharges.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) `ind-b6 a registered company charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) `ind-b6 a registered company charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner`) 1))
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) `ind-b6 a registered company charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- E19-36 for an applicant: notifying it that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed discharges.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 applicant` `a company`) `ind-b6 a registered company charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- E19-37: reported on 2026-02-01, no permission, acts on 2026-03-01, no excuse: contravenes 19(10); offence; one year and a fine with no maximum stated.
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` (`Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE) FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 19(11) the penalty for contravening Article 19(10)` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 12), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
-- E19-38: with a reasonable excuse: contravenes, no offence.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` (`Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE) TRUE
-- E19-39: permitted unconditionally under 19(9)(d): no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` (LIST (`ind-b6 permission` `the Commissioner by written notice to the charity under Article 19(9)(d)` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind-b6 day` TRUE
-- E19-40: permitted on a condition, acts in breach of it: contravenes.
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` (LIST (`ind-b6 permission` `the Commissioner by notice entered in the register under Article 19(9)(e)(ii)` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind-b6 day` FALSE
-- E19-41: permitted by the court under Article 20: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` (LIST (`ind-b6 permission` `the court by an order under Article 20` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind-b6 day` TRUE
-- E19-42: the permission's time limit ended on 2026-02-20: contravenes on 2026-03-01.
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` (LIST (`ind-b6 permission` `the Commissioner by notice entered in the register under Article 19(9)(e)(ii)` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 2 20)))) `ind-b6 day` TRUE
-- E19-43: the 19(9)(d) notice withdrawn on 2026-02-20: contravenes on 2026-03-01.
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` (LIST (`ind-b6 permission` `the Commissioner by written notice to the charity under Article 19(9)(d)` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 20)) NOTHING NOTHING)) `ind-b6 day` TRUE
-- E19-44: reported in 2019, never permitted, acts in 2021: contravenes (no end to the bar but permission).
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 reports` (JUST (YMD 2019 5 1)) (JUST (YMD 2019 5 1)) FALSE) EMPTY (YMD 2021 6 1) TRUE
-- E19-45: an act in contravention of 19(10) is not void or invalid merely for that.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(12) paragraphs (10) and (11) make an act void or invalid merely because it contravened paragraph (10)`
-- E19-46: suspecting a breach of 19(2), the Commissioner MAY apply to the court.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(13) the Commissioner may apply to the court` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 19(13) the Commissioner may apply to the court` TRUE FALSE)

§ `Article 20 -- court orders; disqualification orders (rows E20-01 to E20-25)`

-- E20-01, E20-02, E20-03: on an application under 19(9)(b) or (13), the court may make each listed order; none without an application.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(1)(a) the court may make an order dismissing the application` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(1)(b) the court may make an order giving permission for the governor to act as a governor` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(1)(c) the court may make an order that the entity must not be registered` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(1)(d) the court may make an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(1)(e) the court may make an order making any provision that a required steps notice could make` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(1)(f) the court may make an order ancillary to any such order` TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(1)(a) the court may make an order dismissing the application` FALSE)
-- E20-04: an order for all registered charities, with a time limit: applies to any charity; in force to its last day.
#ASSERT `Art 20(2)(a) the order applies to the charity` (`Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor`, (YMD 2026 1 1), `all registered charities`, (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30))) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `ind-b6 A` (`Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor`, (YMD 2026 1 1), `all registered charities`, (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30))) (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `ind-b6 A` (`Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor`, (YMD 2026 1 1), `all registered charities`, (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30))) (YMD 2026 7 1)
-- E20-05: the Commissioner or the AG may apply for a disqualification order.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `ind-b6 A` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `ind-b6 A` `the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE)
-- E20-06: a governor or anyone else may not.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `ind-b6 A` `a governor` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `ind-b6 A` `any person` TRUE TRUE)
-- E20-07, E20-08: unfit by conduct (as to a registered charity or an applicant): the court MAY make a DO.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- E20-09: unfit by the seriousness of a reportable matter: MAY.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- E20-10: not satisfied the person is unfit: may not.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- E20-11 (convention X): a DO for exactly 15 years from 2020-01-10 (last day 2035-01-10): lawful.
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 10))
-- E20-12: 10 years: lawful.
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2030 1 10))
-- E20-13: 16 years: unlawful.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2036 1 10))
-- E20-14: 15 years and a day: unlawful.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 11))
-- E20-15: an indefinite order (no end; a last day of 9999-12-31 stands in for it): unlawful.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 9999 12 31))
-- E20-16: one year: lawful.
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2021 1 10))
-- E20-17 to E20-19 (convention X, taken): the longest DO from 2020-01-10 ends on 2035-01-10; in force on the 9th and 10th, not the 11th.
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` `ind-b6 A` (YMD 2020 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2035 1 10
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2035 1 10) (`ind-b6 a person with` (LIST (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 10))) FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` (YMD 2035 1 11) (`ind-b6 a person with` (LIST (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 10))) FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
-- E20-20, E20-21 (X with clamp, taken): from 2020-02-29 the longest DO ends on 2035-02-28.
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` `ind-b6 A` (YMD 2020 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2035 2 28
-- E20-22, E20-25: acting as (or being concerned in the management of) a registered charity while the DO binds, without leave: contravenes; offence; 2 years and a fine with no maximum stated.
#ASSERT `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 10)) "A. Innocent" (YMD 2026 10 27) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 20(6) the person commits an offence` (`Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 10)) "A. Innocent" (YMD 2026 10 27) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 20(6) the penalty for contravening a disqualification order` EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
-- E20-23: with the leave of the court: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 10)) "A. Innocent" (YMD 2026 10 27) TRUE TRUE
-- E20-24: after the order has expired: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` (`ind-b6 disqualification order to` (YMD 2035 1 10)) "A. Innocent" (YMD 2036 1 1) TRUE FALSE

§ `Reading checks for Articles 18 to 20 (expected values from each reading's own words)`

-- F6.7 B (every governor bound by 18(2)): a company charity's governor is bound on that reading.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` (`the readings taken but with F6.7 read as` `every governor of a registered charity`) TRUE (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`))
-- F6.24 B (encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other engages): an encourager of an innocent governor.
#ASSERT `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.24 read as` `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`) FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conduct` "B. Encourager" FALSE FALSE (LIST "C. Innocent") FALSE FALSE FALSE), (`ind-b6 conduct` "C. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE)) (`ind-b6 conduct` "B. Encourager" FALSE FALSE (LIST "C. Innocent") FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `ind-b6 A` FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conduct` "B. Encourager" FALSE FALSE (LIST "C. Innocent") FALSE FALSE FALSE), (`ind-b6 conduct` "C. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE)) (`ind-b6 conduct` "B. Encourager" FALSE FALSE (LIST "C. Innocent") FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- F6.9 B (only a disqualification still in force counts): one that ended in 2021 is not a reportable matter in 2026; on the reading taken it is.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` (`the readings taken but with F6.9 read as` `only a disqualification still in force counts`) (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE (LIST `ind-b6 a disqualification that ended in 2021`) EMPTY FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` `ind-b6 A` (YMD 2026 1 1) (`ind-b6 a person with` EMPTY FALSE (LIST `ind-b6 a disqualification that ended in 2021`) EMPTY FALSE EMPTY FALSE)
-- F6.11 B (19(11) reaches 19(8)): the penalty of 19(8) is that of 19(11).
#ASSERT `Art 19(8) the penalty for contravening Article 19(8)` (`the readings taken but with F6.11 read as` `Article 19(11) reaches paragraph (8) as well`) EQUALS (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 12), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`)
-- F6.10 B (the ban starts on the report to the charity): reported to the charity only, the governor is barred on that reading, not on the reading taken.
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts on the report to the entity or charity`) TRUE (`ind-b6 reports` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) NOTHING FALSE) EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 reports` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) NOTHING FALSE) EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE
-- F6.22 B (the permission ends before the day named): acting on the last day of a time limit contravenes on that reading.
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.22 read as` `the permission ends before the day named`) TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` (LIST (`ind-b6 permission` `the Commissioner by notice entered in the register under Article 19(9)(e)(ii)` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)))) `ind-b6 day` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE `ind-b6 reported on 1 February 2026` (LIST (`ind-b6 permission` `the Commissioner by notice entered in the register under Article 19(9)(e)(ii)` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)))) `ind-b6 day` TRUE
-- F6.14 B and C (the fifteen years: roll; the day before the anniversary): A-08.
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`) (YMD 2020 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2035 3 1
#ASSERT `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) (YMD 2020 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2035 1 9
-- F6.23 B (either officer's view lets both apply): the Commissioner may apply on the AG's view alone on that reading, not on the reading taken.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` (`the readings taken but with F6.23 read as` `the view of either the Commissioner or the Attorney General`) `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `ind-b6 A` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE)
-- F6.16 B (a year is 365 days) against A (12 calendar months): a 366-day term from 2028-01-01 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` `ind-b6 A` (YMD 2028 1 1) 366
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` (`the readings taken but with F6.16 read as` `days`) (YMD 2028 1 1) 366

§ `Reading checks for G6 added at review (F6.8 B, F6.10 C, F6.12 B/C, F6.15 A/B/C, F6.20 B, F6.21 B)`

-- F6.8 A (taken) and B: a governor who actively conceals, but not beyond a reasonable time, engages in misconduct on A and not on B.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 alone, misconduct of` FALSE (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.8 read as` `the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps`) FALSE (LIST (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE)) (`ind-b6 conduct` "A. Innocent" FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- F6.10 C (the ban starts when both reports are made): reported to the Commissioner only, no ban on C; a ban on the reading taken.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (`the readings taken but with F6.10 read as` `the ban starts when both reports have been made`) TRUE (`ind-b6 reports` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) FALSE) EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (`ind-b6 reports` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) FALSE) EMPTY `ind-b6 day` TRUE
-- F6.12 B (30 days from the matter arising) and C (30 days from awareness), on 2026-02-05, nothing reported: in breach on B (35 days), not on C (16 days).
#ASSERT `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 2 5) (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`)) `ind-b6 an unreported matter learned of late`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`) (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 2 5) (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`)) `ind-b6 an unreported matter learned of late`
-- F6.12 B with no number supplied: the Law gives none, so the question refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.12 read as` `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`) NOTHING (YMD 2026 2 5) (`ind-b6 governor` "G. Brown" (LIST `bankruptcy or other insolvency`)) `ind-b6 an unreported matter learned of late`
-- F6.15 A (taken): for an organized religious charity no duty to require removal arises: serving a removal notice does not discharge 19(9)(e); a permission does.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) `ind-b6 an organized religious charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner`) 1))
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) `ind-b6 an organized religious charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- F6.15 B (the duty stands, the notice void to that extent): serving the removal notice discharges it.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` (`the readings taken but with F6.15 read as` `the duty stands and the notice is void to the extent that it requires removal`) (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) `ind-b6 an organized religious charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- F6.15 C (a conflict the Law does not resolve): the trace refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` (`the readings taken but with F6.15 read as` `the two provisions conflict and the Law does not say which prevails`) (`ind-b6 entity` `ind-b6 general` `a company`) `ind-b6 an organized religious charity` (`ind-b6 reported matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- F6.20 B (an earlier day is needed): a declaration on the day of the application is in time on the reading taken, not on B.
#ASSERT `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` `ind-b6 A` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 10)) (YMD 2026 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` (`the readings taken but with F6.20 read as` `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 10)) (YMD 2026 1 10)
-- F6.21 A (taken) and B: notified on 2026-02-01, no declaration on 2026-02-02, a reasonable time not yet passed: in breach on A, not on B.
#ASSERT `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` `ind-b6 A` TRUE (YMD 2026 2 2) (`ind-b6 governor` "H. Clean" EMPTY) (`Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)), NOTHING, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` (`the readings taken but with F6.21 read as` `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`) TRUE (YMD 2026 2 2) (`ind-b6 governor` "H. Clean" EMPTY) (`Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)), NOTHING, FALSE)
